    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(2) Section 6",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976#sec-6-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976.pdf, p.2",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The person who was, immediately before the commencement of\nthis Act, the Chairman of the Commission continues to be the Chairman\nof the Commission as if he had been appointed as the Chairman under\nthe Principal Act as amended by this Act and holds office, subject to the\nPrincipal Act as amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of\nhis appointment under the Principal Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The person who was, immediately before the commencement of\nthis Act, the Chairman of the Commission continues to be the Chairman\nof the Commission as if he had been appointed as the Chairman under\nthe Principal Act as amended by this Act and holds office, subject to the\nPrincipal Act as amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of\nhis appointment under the Principal Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "41aa7208cb0a57aee239244eb8d0e8d71dd7168dc3a8953558c260ba11f267fe",
      "skos:note": "Continuation of Chairman's office upon commencement of Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976#sec-6-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(2) Section 6",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 2,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The person who was, immediately before the commencement of\nthis Act, the Chairman of the Commission continues to be the Chairman\nof the Commission as if he had been appointed as the Chairman under\nthe Principal Act as amended by this Act and holds office, subject to the\nPrincipal Act as amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of\nhis appointment under the Principal Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "continues",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to hold office",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(3) Section 6",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976#sec-6-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976.pdf, p.2",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person who held office as a Commissioner other than the\nChairman immediately before the commencement of this Act continues\nto hold office as a Commissioner as if he had been appointed as a Com­\nmissioner under the Principal Act as amended by this Act and, if he was\nappointed for a specified period, holds office, subject to the Principal Act\nas amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of his appoint­\nment under the Principal Act.\n\nAustralian Heritage Commission Amendment\nNo. 135\n7.\nSection 23 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the end Entry of\nthereof the following sub-section: —\nRegister\n“ (5) The Commission shall not take any action under this section in\nrelation to a place for reasons relating only to the association of the place\nwith the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals unless—\n(a) the place is a site specially protected under a law of a State or\nTerritory by reason of its association with the history, culture or\nbeliefs of Aboriginals; or\n(b) the action is taken in accordance with a direction of the Minister\nunder section 25 or the recommendation of a person or\norganization approved by the Minister for the purposes of this\nsub-section.”.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A person who held office as a Commissioner other than the\nChairman immediately before the commencement of this Act continues\nto hold office as a Commissioner as if he had been appointed as a Com­\nmissioner under the Principal Act as amended by this Act and, if he was\nappointed for a specified period, holds office, subject to the Principal Act\nas amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of his appoint­\nment under the Principal Act.\n\nAustralian Heritage Commission Amendment\nNo. 135\n7.\nSection 23 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the end Entry of\nthereof the following sub-section: —\nRegister\n“ (5) The Commission shall not take any action under this section in\nrelation to a place for reasons relating only to the association of the place\nwith the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals unless—\n(a) the place is a site specially protected under a law of a State or\nTerritory by reason of its association with the history, culture or\nbeliefs of Aboriginals; or\n(b) the action is taken in accordance with a direction of the Minister\nunder section 25 or the recommendation of a person or\norganization approved by the Minister for the purposes of this\nsub-section.”.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d4c0bbef9b9812a27c1dc97cfc667a495c25ed1f54757a10882af9e2fd42799c",
      "skos:note": "A person who held office as a Commissioner continues to hold office."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976#sec-6-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(3) Section 6",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 2,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person who held office as a Commissioner other than the\nChairman immediately before the commencement of this Act continues\nto hold office as a Commissioner as if he had been appointed as a Com­\nmissioner under the Principal Act as amended by this Act and, if he was\nappointed for a specified period, holds office, subject to the Principal Act\nas amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of his appoint­\nment under the Principal Act.\n\nAustralian Heritage Commission Amendment\nNo. 135\n7.\nSection 23 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the end Entry of\nthereof the following sub-section: —\nRegister\n“ (5) The Commission shall not take any action under this section in\nrelation to a place for reasons relating only to the association of the place\nwith the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals unless—\n(a) the place is a site specially protected under a law of a State or\nTerritory by reason of its association with the history, culture or\nbeliefs of Aboriginals; or\n(b) the action is taken in accordance with a direction of the Minister\nunder section 25 or the recommendation of a person or\norganization approved by the Minister for the purposes of this\nsub-section.”."
    },
    {
